# H1 `models2`: a model released while the binary runs. The catalog has one
# model until the `models2` line, after the first `/model` is closed, and two
# from there on; `/model` is opened before and after, and the gateway log says
# which ask got which catalog, and when. Until FLAKE-HINT4 r2 the switch was
# fixed at 9 s after the gateway started. By that clock the launch's ask came
# at 0.8 to 4.4 s on most runs on record, but at 9.9 s (xfx) and 14.3 s (fx)
# on a loaded one, which the fixed switch would have answered with the second
# catalog before the first `/model`. fx asks again at the second `/model`,
# xfx at launch only, and no binary asks between the two, so this line gives
# each ask what the unloaded runs gave it.
models h1-models-one.json
wait 4
type /model
key Enter
wait 2
snap before
key Escape
wait 6
models2 h1-models-two.json
type /model
key Enter
wait 3
snap after
key Escape
wait 0.5
gwlog
